# free5gc/udm CVE-2026-33191 (GHSA-p9hg-pq3q-v9gv): the Nudm_SubscriberDataManagement
# handlers read the SUPI or UE ID straight from the gin route path and forward it
# into the processor layer with no format validation. The identifier grammars
# (TS 23.003 / TS 29.571) forbid control characters, so a route value carrying a
# null byte (URL-encoded %00) travels through the UDR client construction and
# NRF discovery until Go's net/url rejects it -- "invalid control character in
# URL" -- and the failure surfaces as a 500 instead of a 400.
#
# The advisory's fix is PR free5gc/udm#79 (88de9fa74a1b3f3522e53b4cfa2d184712ffa4ee,
# a merge whose combined diff is empty; `git diff 9308405 88de9fa` reads it in
# full). It adds the free5gc util validator in front of the forwarding in four
# handlers -- HandleGetAmData gains `if !validator.IsValidSupi(supi) { ...400...;
# return }`, and HandleUnsubscribe, HandleModify and HandleGetIdTranslationResult
# gain `valid := validator.IsValidGpsi(ueId) || validator.IsValidSupi(ueId)` --
# and bumps github.com/free5gc/util to the revision carrying the validator
# package. The pool row named 65d7070f, PR #78, which is a different fix (the
# SDM-notify 204 nil guard); the advisory references 88de9fa.
#
# The pool-row commit and the fixing change both leave API-documented calls inside
# the guarded functions, which is the counterweight that makes this detectable
# without keying on the fixed revision's own helpers: free5gc's util/validator is a
# documented library (one format validator per 3GPP identifier, each explicitly
# rejecting null bytes), and the handler side keys on the standard identifier
# names the route registration carries.
#
# Detection is code.UnvalidatedRouteIdentifier (VYQL-VAL-036, CWE-20/158/248),
# a new concept for the weakness class "a request-supplied standard-identifier
# route parameter is forwarded into request processing without the ecosystem's
# documented format validator in the handling function", emitted by
# sbiRouteIdentifierForwardedWithoutValidator in
# vyql/bindings/go/sbiRouteIdentifierValidation.vyql. The same file labels the
# validator package's calls as core.InputValidation checks, so taint rules that
# honour InputValidation respect free5gc identifier validation from now on.
#
# Measured with `--cache off` over three runs per revision. The whole udm tree
# at the vulnerable parent 9308405 reports 32 VYQL-VAL-036 rows (32/32/32)
# across six SBI handler files -- subscriberdatamanagement 15,
# uecontextmanagement 8, ueauthentication 4, eventexposure 3, parameterprovision
# 1, httpcallback 1 -- for 47 findings total against a 15-finding baseline, so
# the rule adds its 32 rows and moves nothing else. At the fixed revision 88de9fa it
# reports 28 (28/28/28), and the four rows the fixed revision's own handlers carried are
# gone -- HandleGetAmData, HandleUnsubscribe, HandleModify,
# HandleGetIdTranslationResult. The remaining 28 are handlers the fixed revision does not
# touch and that still forward supi/ueId unvalidated at that revision, which is
# the advisory's "all endpoints that include path parameters". The 500/400
# null-byte story is unchanged in them.
#
# Collateral, enumerated by grep rather than sampled: across every clone under
# /tmp/cve-work/rank*/ the identifier-narrowed shape (a gin route-param read of
# supi/ueId/gpsi/suci/pei) exists only in the two free5gc trees -- this udm
# checkout and the sibling udr clone, whose api_datarepository.go carries 60
# such reads and zero validator calls anywhere in the tree; scanning it reports
# exactly those 60 rows (60/60/60), all in that one file. Two non-free5gc Go
# trees scan to zero rows for the rule: traefik, and the free5gc umbrella
# repository, whose checked-out tree is build scripts and webconsole code with
# no SBI handlers. Removing the identifier-name clause would drop the binding
# back onto every gin handler in the world, since the negation can only be
# satisfied by free5gc's own validators.

test "rank1884: an sdm handler forwards the supi route parameter with no identifier validator"
  lang go
  file internal/sbi/api_subscriberdatamanagement.go
  expect VYQL-VAL-036
  expect_review code.UnvalidatedRouteIdentifier
  code
  ```
  package sbi

  import (
  	"net/http"
  	"net/url"

  	"github.com/free5gc/openapi/models"
  	"github.com/free5gc/udm/internal/logger"
  	"github.com/gin-gonic/gin"
  )

  // GetAmData - retrieve a UE's Access and Mobility Subscription Data
  func (s *Server) HandleGetAmData(c *gin.Context) {
  	query := url.Values{}
  	query.Set("plmn-id", c.Query("plmn-id"))
  	query.Set("supported-features", c.Query("supported-features"))

  	plmnID := query.Get("plmn-id")
  	supportedFeatures := query.Get("supported-features")

  	logger.SdmLog.Infof("Handle GetAmData")

  	supi := c.Params.ByName("supi")

  	s.Processor().GetAmDataProcedure(c, supi, plmnID, supportedFeatures)
  }
  ```
  file go.mod
  code
  ```
